From b3764995a3be1434815d0b84097c6e0a086ce4ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:16:23 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] FFmpeg: libavformat and libswresample, for host audio
 files

Host audio files (MP3, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, FLAC, WAV) need a demuxer and a
resampler besides libavcodec. The Windows build (BtbN's LGPL shared
build) already ships avformat-61.dll and swresample-5.dll with every
native decoder; avformat-61.dll is now copied next to the executable and
both are linked. The source build for macOS, Linux and Android now
builds libavformat and libswresample too, with only the wav, mp3, ogg
and flac demuxers, the mpegaudio, vorbis, opus and flac parsers, and the
mp3float, vorbis, opus, flac and PCM decoders added to the ATRAC and
H.264 ones; no protocol (files are read through the host's own I/O), no
filter, scaler, device or network code. Still LGPL-2.1-or-later only,
which the build checks as before. The changed flags rebuild FFmpeg once.

PORTABLEKIT_FFMPEG_HOST_AUDIO says whether the two libraries are there
(PORTABLEKIT_HAS_HOST_AUDIO for the code). With PORTABLEKIT_FFMPEG=system
they are optional: without them music and movies work as before and
host audio files are not played.

The packaging lists (Windows, macOS, Android), the desktop app's notices
and SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md name the two libraries and the new flags. A
port's own THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md must carry the new configure line for
the release scripts' check.

Verified on Windows (MSVC, the prebuilt build): two builds of one port
link and run, and decode MP3, Vorbis, Opus, FLAC and WAV files. Not
verified: the source build on macOS, Linux and Android (configure and
make were not run), the system mode, the release scripts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
